2
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,050
I love it! I love it!

3
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,400
-Yes. -Ha-ha-ha.

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,740
I knew that'd get him! -Hey.

5
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:52,550
Hello? MAN : Walter?

6
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:55,430
Yes? -I have some bad news.

7
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,600
It's about your two uncles, son.

8
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,770
Walter?

9
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:04,940
Walter? Walter.

10
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:06,400
Good news.

11
00:01:06,570 --> 00:01:09,150
You're spending the summer with your two uncles.

12
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:14,950
It's just gonna be for a few weeks. A month or two, tops.

13
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,870
Scout's honor, okay?

14
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:22,920
Cross my heart and hope to die, okay?

15
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:26,210
Where are you going this time?

16
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:29,670
The Fort Worth College of Court Reporting.

17
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,180
I met a guy last night.

18
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:33,340
He's gonna pull some strings.

19
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:38,810
Walter, you're gonna have to learn to trust people...

20
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:41,940
...or you're gonna grow up bitter and disappointed.

21
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:47,150
You're gonna have fun with your two uncles. You'll see.

22
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,320
Mom, you're an only child.

23
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:51,990
I know what uncles are.

24
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:55,990
Well, Mr. Smarty-Pants...

25
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:59,040
...it just so happens, they really are your uncles.

26
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:01,000
Your great-uncles.

27
00:02:01,170 --> 00:02:03,000
My mother's brothers.

28
00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:04,500
They disappeared 40 years ago...

29
00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:06,750
...and just now showed up back here in Texas.

30
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,880
-Can't I come with you? -No.

31
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:14,890
Honey, I'm gonna be working my tail off learning court reporting.

32
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:17,850
I'm doing everything I can to keep this family together.

33
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:20,520
How about a little help here, okay?

34
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:27,650
Now, look.

35
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:32,740
They say these two old men got millions stashed away in cash.

36
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:34,860
Nobody knows where they got it.

37
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:38,410
Got no kids, no one to leave all that money to.

38
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:41,080
You and me, we're as close as any family they got.

39
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,290
You want them to like me...

40
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:48,420
...so they'll die and leave us their money?

41
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:52,880
We could buy a house, maybe settle down.

42
00:02:53,050 --> 00:02:55,590
Wouldn't that be nice?

43
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:58,470
Oh, look. Here it is.

44
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:01,140
Here it is, honey. Here it is.

45
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:07,900
By the way, I hear these two were in some state nuthouse for 40 years.

46
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:10,070
Got all their money from a big lawsuit or something.

47
00:03:10,230 --> 00:03:13,400
But then there's lots of stories about them.

48
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:15,610
Who knows what to believe?

49
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:20,240
Just find out where they stashed all that money, okay?

50
00:03:20,410 --> 00:03:26,460
-Maybe we should've called first. -No. Older people just love surprises.

51
00:03:27,210 --> 00:03:29,040
Here we are.

52
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:33,260
Okay.

53
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,430
Aah! Aah!

54
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:44,850
Go away, go away. Hey, go away. Shoo.

55
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:49,770
Show them you're friendly, honey. Let them smell your hand.

56
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,280
They must be down there by that lake.

57
00:03:57,450 --> 00:03:59,910
Let's go. Come on.

58
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:04,290
Let's go. There he is.

59
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,500
Winged him. GARTH: He's running for it.

60
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:15,840
Damn. Empty. -Get ammo. I'll keep him covered.

61
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:17,050
Yoo-hoo.

62
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:18,550
Ha, ha.

63
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,510
Huh?

64
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,810
Yoo-hoo.

65
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:26,230
You send for a hooker?

66
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:29,100
Uncle Hub, Uncle Garth, it's me, Mae.

67
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:34,150
Mae.

68
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:37,990
Pearl's daughter.

69
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:41,700
And I brought Walter, your nephew.

70
00:04:43,410 --> 00:04:46,160
-Relatives. -Damn, God.

71
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,460
We're old, damn it. Leave us alone.

72
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,670
The last thing we need is some little sissy boy...

73
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,920
...hanging around all summer.

74
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:56,840
Walter, honey...

75
00:04:57,010 --> 00:05:00,090
...why don't you wait out here and play, okay? I'll be a minute.

76
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:11,730
He could help out around here, do chores.

77
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:14,360
Help out? Your kid's a damn wienie.

78
00:05:14,530 --> 00:05:15,570
I know.

79
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:18,030
That's why he needs to be around real men...

80
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:21,700
...like you two. It won't be for long.

81
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:24,870
He's gotta cook for his damn self. I'm not cooking.

82
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:35,840
Nice doggie. Come play.

83
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,920
This is for your own good, Walter.

84
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,300
You know...

85
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:44,050
... I bet all that money is hidden real close by.

86
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:45,970
Imagine, a real buried treasure...

87
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,270
...just like in those books you're always reading.

88
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:54,230
Walter, maybe if you'd learn to smile once in a while...

89
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,610
...then people might like you.

90
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:01,740
Now, come on, how about a big smile to remember you by?

91
00:06:01,910 --> 00:06:04,700
Okay? Come on.

92
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:13,170
You're gonna have to work on that smile while I'm gone, okay?

93
00:06:16,210 --> 00:06:19,210
Bye, honey. Bye.

94
00:06:41,450 --> 00:06:42,700
Well?

95
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:16,310
If my mom calls, can we hear the telephone out here?

96
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,690
-Don't have one. -No telephone?

97
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:27,530
Is it okay if I go inside and watch television?

98
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:31,790
-Ain't got one. -No television?

99
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:35,000
What do you do?

100
00:07:49,350 --> 00:07:51,220
Hey.

101
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:56,100
Rumor has is you two have millions stashed away.

102
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:58,440
Why not put some of that money to work for you...

103
00:07:58,610 --> 00:08:02,110
...with the high yield only investing in gold and silver can bring?

104
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,490
Can I leave you some pamphlets?

105
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,890
Gentlemen, word is out.

106
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:38,230
You are two sophisticated men of means--

107
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,230
Hey!

108
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:16,970
Nice evening. Peaceful.

